{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1562624-deviant-night-horrors-deep-dive-beta-read","id":1562624,"title":"Deviant Night Horrors: Deep Dive Beta Read","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Deviant: The Renegades"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-08-04T04:36:58-07:00","id":1562624,"title":"Deviant Night Horrors: Deep Dive Beta Read","content":"The beta read of *Deep Dive* has started. For the next two months, I'll be sharing long excerpts of this work in progress (with patrons having access to the full text). The first excerpt, which includes the list of chapters in this book, is <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/Dayzdark/posts/deep-dive-beta-165705857?utm_medium=clipboard_copy&amp;utm_source=copyLink&amp;utm_campaign=postshare_creator&amp;utm_content=join_link\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. Here is the list of the 40 conspiracies it contains:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Gustaw's Retinue (Standing 1):</b> The operatives, support staff, and bodyguards who have taken it upon themselves to protect and elevate Gustaw Bernhard, a billionaire celebrity-businessman.<br /> <br /> <b>Neighborhood Watch (Standing 1):</b> A band of stochastic vigilantes who fight crime in their neighborhood.<br /> <br /> <b>Ratcatchers Union (Standing 1):</b> An overzealous extermination company that roams campgrounds and rural areas selling its services and abducting test subjects for its chemical pesticides.<br /> <br /> <b>Tavayana (Standing 1):</b> A New Age clinic whose guided meditations have addictive and occult properties.<br /> <br /> <b>Twelve Mile (Standing 1):</b> A tiny town under the thumb of a young Divergence scientist studying the transformative properties of the nearby quarry lake.<br /> <br /> <b>Brantley Consortium (Standing 2):</b> An organized crime ring that supplies an occult means of translocation to thieves in the local underworld.<br /> <br /> <b>Dark Matter Fellowship (Standing 2):</b> A group of graduate students at a research university who have developed a means of interacting with materials and beings comprised of dark matter that coexist with humans on Earth.<br /> <br /> <b>Iverson Funeral Home (Standing 2):</b> A family-run mortuary in a small town whose proprietors pursue immortality through necromancy.<br /> <br /> <b>Lebeau Family (Standing 2):</b> Farmers living near a creek whose mystical properties have inextricably bound them to the Remade they lure into their service.<br /> <br /> <b>Parents of Psychic Children (Standing 2):</b> A support network that advocates for parents as they navigate the challenges of raising a psychic child.<br /> <br /> <b>Aura Experts Incorporated (Standing 3):</b> An urban planning consulting firm that uses Divergences to redirect the flow of ley lines to the benefit of their clients and themselves.<br /> <br /> <b>Corvalis Chemicals (Standing 3):</b> A chemical company that offers other conspiracies Divergence-for-hire services and a spray-on compound that compels the obedience of nearby Remade.<br /> <br /> <b>Next-Gen LE (Standing 3):</b> A tech start-up that provides AI-driven solutions for law enforcement that it claims can produce predictive, models of human behavior.<br /> <br /> <b>Whisper Vault (Standing 3):</b> Collectors of stories who support their work by acting as information brokers and protect their interests by means of blackmail.<br /> <br /> <b>Enchanting Anomalies (Standing 4):</b> A talent agency specializing in performers with strange and disturbing appearances.<br /> <br /> <b>Handel-Upton Group (Standing 4):</b> A real estate partnership that increases the value of their properties by using its low-income tenants to carry away evil spirits.<br /> <br /> <b>Project ICELVS (Standing 4):</b> A government program studying the intelligence-gathering potential of dreams.<br /> <br /> <b>Apokalupsis Phaidimos (Standing 5):</b> A network of seers and psychics who wish to unmask the secret sins of the powerful.<br /> <br /> <b>Malleo in Draconis (Standing 5):</b> A cult dedicated to Saint Margaret of Antioch that hunts monsters, especially dragons and demons.<br /> <br /> <b>Nippon Collective (Standing 5):</b> An order of psychics, mystics, and mediums who act as peacekeepers between humanity and the unseen world.<br /> <br /> <b>Cult of Serapsis (Standing 6):</b> A fractious cult seeking the resurrection of a long-dead god.<br /> <br /> <b>PIETA (Standing 6):</b> Mercenaries and bounty hunters who specialize in capturing hard-to-catch Deviants for the conspiracies of the Web of Pain, law enforcement, organized crime and even Renegades looking to settle a score with another Deviant.<br /> <br /> <b>Redfield (Standing 6):</b> A conglomerate of agricultural companies exploiting land across the globe through industrialized megafarms, and a constellation of R&amp;D and post-harvest processing businesses.<br /> <br /> <b>Humane Acquisitions (Standing 7):</b> A biotech conglomerate with roots in organized crime that traffics in human organs and illicit medical experimentation.<br /> <br /> <b>Kindly Ones (Standing 7):</b> A loose alliance of Renegade cohorts determined to make participation in the Web of Pain so dangerous and expensive that conspiracy agents abandon their ambitions.<br /> <br /> <b>Righteous (Standing 7):</b> The genocidal cult devoted to a devil of cruelty and xenophobia.<br /> <br /> <b>Extraordinary Leagues Federation (Standing 8):</b> Sports organizers that promote and popularize competitions between Deviants.<br /> <br /> <b>Kingmakers Sodality (Standing 8):</b> A secret society with roots in the Medieval Church that supports the divine right of kings to rule over ordinary people.<br /> <br /> <b>Magorum Collegia (Standing 8):</b> A global guild of sorcerers who practice and attempt to regulate summoning magic, especially summoning magic that draws on the power of ephemeral entities.<br /> <br /> <b>Global Quality Capital (Standing 9):</b> A venture capital conglomerate with a vast and diverse portfolio of businesses, including Web of Pain conspiracies, which it regards as just another asset to be acquired and exploited.<br /> <br /> <b>The Holography (Standing 9):</b> A conspiracy of scientists, artists, and cultists who attempt to harness an incomprehensible otherworldly force with an alien intelligence behind it.<br /> <br /> <b>The Old Boys Club (Standing 9):</b> A loose network of immortal billionaires who use their wealth and eternal life to indulge their whims.<br /> <br /> <b>Stargazers (Standing 9):</b> Earthly agents of a hostile extraterrestrial empire who work to prime humanity for easy conquest by the coming invasion force.<br /> <br /> <b>Terroir (Standing 9):</b> Strange phenomena that recur all over the world that are but echoes of the bizarre world from which they emanate.<br /> <br /> <b>Fahr Colonies (Standing 10):</b> A colonial power from Earth bent on conquest of an otherworldly fantasy world and its peoples.<br /> <br /> <b>Round Order (Standing 10):</b> Invaders from an otherworld where Remade have supplanted Baselines as rulers.<br /> <br /> <b>Symposium (Standing 10):</b> Visitors from one of humanity's possible futures working tirelessly to bootstrap themselves into power earlier in the timeline.<br /> <br /> <b>The Tenth Choir (Standing 10):</b> Ambitious eugenicists whose supreme ambition is to replace the God-Machine and its servants with the angels they create.<br /> <br /> <b>The Trahern Syndicate (Standing 10):</b> An organization that has built a base of operations in the Hedge to study changelings and other Fae phenomena.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}